## Cause and smallest correction

The pinned original `card-1.110.0/lib/card/rule/cache.rb` selects only live
rules whose left card is Set-typed and right card is Setting-typed. Its lookup
key also requires the setting and pattern codenames. A matching compound name
is insufficient. The selected production correctly enforces those conditions;
the three older fixtures did not construct qualifying rules.

- Head/page fixture: `*all` and `*layout` were Basic-typed, and no Setting type
  existed. The layout rule is correctly excluded; the page then takes the
  default layout, which references the absent `header` codename. Setup now
  declares Cardtype/Set/Setting type anchors, Set-types `*all`, and Setting-types
  `*layout`. It does not add `header` to hide the unintended layout fallback.
- Type-event fixture: the `Widget+*right` set and `*structure` setting both
  used arbitrary type ID 14. Setup now uses the existing standard fixture's
  registered Set ID and declares/uses a registered Setting type for the tag.
  The original structured-type refusal and create/update assertions remain.
- Pointer fixture: the `*input type` tag had neither Setting type nor its
  codename; `*self` had no pattern codename. Setup now supplies the Setting type
  and relevant setting/pattern codenames, including correctly typed read/update
  tags. It preserves the existing Set trunk, rule value, filler population,
  selected value and exact 100-option/default-limit assertions.

There is no production change or qualification exception. Test bodies from
the first `describe(` to EOF are byte-identical to the exact parent in all
three files; their hashes are retained in `compat176-assertion-custody.json`.

The head fixture also carries the parent's existing explicit
`new ModLoader(..., s.engine.views)` binding. This one line already exists in
both root pins; it is not a new issue176 behavior change. The retained fixer
branch lacked it. Intermediate executions using that older test setup produced
six UnsupportedViewError failures; those logs remain diagnostic failures, not
acceptance. Final controls pin all helpers and retain the root binding.

## Qualification and security controls

An additional unchanged, Git-pinned selection of eight rule test files executes
36 cases through the exact experimental production. All pass with zero skips
or failures. It covers Set/Setting rejection, setting/pattern codename mutation,
requested cache keys with both stored-key fallback modes, receiving-engine
pattern names, independent pattern boundaries, trash and ordinary-save
revocation, and ten comparisons with actual original Ruby rule SQL/methods.

The native comparisons use Ruby 3.4.11 and card 1.110.0 with the existing
minimal SQLite-backed Card adapters. They do not boot Rails, ActiveRecord,
mod registration or RSpec, and do not establish fresh native-framework or
release acceptance. All ten source observations were retained; the original
rule-cache source SHA-256 is
`17a240a32aed7c2ea07c69df21bfb78190a4cd501583171f2b23403de1f7736d`.
The original type validation and options/default-limit source were inspected
directly; no live reference, VM, install or provider call was made.

The temporary exact Git-pinned Ruby probe was removed after its bytes were
verified against the experimental ref. Native observations were copied and
byte-verified into retained evidence before their temporary output was removed.
Each native fixture DB was closed and removed by the unchanged control. No
fixture DB directory remained. No new checkout, build directory or server was
created. Earlier issues 154/156/164/170/174 remain separate packages.

